      "result": {
        "summary": "Reviewed full diff (spawn.py, decision_log.py, promotion.py, memory_hot.py, memory_store.py, daemon.py, pool.toml, docs, and 4 new test classes) against acceptance criteria. Shadow mode presents legacy sections byte-identical to off mode (verified via test assertion shadow==legacy); active mode substitutes tiered HOT+WARM content bounded by packet_hot_tokens, falling through the existing 4800-char trim afterward with no second cap. Packet building never calls memory_hot.build(); only the daemon does, once per tick under memory_hot.BUILD_LOCK, gated by mtime-based freshness (HOT.md >= index.sqlite). decision_log already had an unused 'retrieval' CONTEXT_KINDS entry, correctly reused (not duplicated) with a docstring note. promotion.py registers memory_tiers with the same global CRITERIA (no bespoke threshold), collect() sums retrieval-row tokens and computes fix_rounds_delta from bus fix_round_for counts, returning None until both cohorts have >=5 tasks. WAL/busy_timeout added to memory_store._open. Retrieval logging and tiered retrieval are both wrapped in try/except with a logged warning so failures cannot break packet construction. Ran the 8 new unittest methods plus the full test_spawn/test_decision_log/test_promotion/test_daemon/test_memory_hot/test_memory_store suites (385 tests) \u2014 all green. No defects found.",
